    <section id="about">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">About me</span>
            <h2>I bring a systems mindset to every search problem.</h2>
            <p>
              My Bachelor of Computer Application foundation in programming, data structures, and algorithms
              shapes the way I approach SEO. I look for relationships between entities, pages, queries, systems,
              and business outcomes—not isolated checklist items.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-grid">
          <article class="panel">
            <h3>Where I create value</h3>
            <ul class="list">
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>Strategy that connects the whole site</b><p>I map search intent, entities, page types, content depth, and internal links so the architecture supports the business.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>Execution across the SEO journey</b><p>I work across on-page, technical, off-page, content, local, e-commerce, reporting, and automation requirements.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>Search that is ready for what comes next</b><p>I use structured data, AEO, GEO, llms.txt, and LLM tracking to prepare brands for changing search experiences.</p></div></li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="panel">
            <h3>How I operate</h3>
            <ul class="list">
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>I start with evidence</b><p>I use Search Console, GA4, crawl data, analytics, and business context before I recommend a rewrite, migration, or campaign.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>I make the work repeatable</b><p>I turn useful insights into templates, rules, dashboards, scripts, and workflows that teams can actually use.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>I report with context</b><p>I explain what changed, why it changed, what I did, and what I expect to happen next.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="bullet"></span><div><b>I lead delivery</b><p>I have managed and supported a 50+ member team across SEO, design, development, QA, and client communication.</p></div></li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>

        <article class="panel about-photo" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <img src="assets/bibek-khatiwada-portrait.png" alt="Bibek Khatiwada overlooking Kathmandu" loading="lazy">
          <div>
            <div class="mini-note">the person behind the systems</div>
            <h3 style="margin-top:.65rem">I’m Bibek Khatiwada, an SEO strategist who connects search, systems, and execution.</h3>
            <p style="margin-top:.7rem">I’m based in Kathmandu, Nepal, and open to remote work. Over 3+ years, I progressed from SEO Intern to SEO Executive, SEO Specialist, Team Lead, and SEO Strategist. I’ve worked across 150+ projects, 100+ niches, 10+ live sites, and clients in six countries.</p>
            <p style="margin-top:.7rem">My Bachelor of Computer Application foundation in programming, data structures, and algorithms shapes how I solve SEO problems. I combine entity-based SEO, topical authority, technical audits, on-page and off-page execution, content systems, automation, reporting, and AI search optimization.</p>
            <div class="about-detail-list">
              <div><b>My leadership</b><span>I have managed and supported a 50+ member team across SEO, design, development, QA, and client communication.</span></div>
              <div><b>My operating range</b><span>I have handled 60+ client accounts concurrently while maintaining structured delivery and transparent reporting.</span></div>
              <div><b>My technical side</b><span>I build n8n and Python workflows, Apps Script systems, plugins, extensions, crawlers, dashboards, and LLM-assisted tools.</span></div>
              <div><b>My working style</b><span>I start with evidence, turn insights into repeatable actions, and explain the reasoning behind every priority.</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="panel" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <div class="mini-note">career timeline</div>
          <div class="timeline">
            <div class="timeline-row"><div class="timeline-year">2021</div><div><div class="timeline-role">SEO Intern</div><p class="timeline-note">Built the foundation in on-page SEO, keyword research, and client delivery.</p></div></div>
            <div class="timeline-row"><div class="timeline-year">2022</div><div><div class="timeline-role">SEO Executive</div><p class="timeline-note">Expanded into off-page SEO, technical audits, and independent campaign management.</p></div></div>
            <div class="timeline-row"><div class="timeline-year">2023</div><div><div class="timeline-role">SEO Specialist</div><p class="timeline-note">Moved deeper into data analysis, entity-based SEO, and repeatable workflows.</p></div></div>
            <div class="timeline-row"><div class="timeline-year">2024 — now</div><div><div class="timeline-role">RankMeTop · Team Lead → SEO Strategist</div><p class="timeline-note">I progressed into end-to-end strategy across 150+ projects, 100+ niches, six countries, and a 50+ member team.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="research">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Research & method</span>
            <h2>I use research to make implementation more precise.</h2>
            <p>I combine SEO practice with programming, NLP, knowledge graphs, query processing, and AI-assisted search to plan work that is easier to explain and execute.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-grid">
          <article class="research-card">
            <div class="label">Published research</div>
            <h3>I study how search systems understand meaning.</h3>
            <p>I use ideas from NLP, knowledge graphs, query processing, and AI-assisted search to understand how engines interpret entities, relationships, and intent.</p>
            <div class="frameworks">
              <div class="framework"><b>Cognitive Search</b><span>How NLP, machine learning, and knowledge graphs change organic visibility.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Query Processing</b><span>How engines interpret, expand, and rewrite queries before ranking pages.</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="research-card">
            <div class="label">Frameworks in practice</div>
            <h3>I turn strategy into named, repeatable systems.</h3>
            <div class="frameworks">
              <div class="framework"><b>Query Deserves a Page</b><span>Decide whether a URL should exist before writing content.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Entity–Attribute–Value</b><span>Structure pages around extractable relationships, not loose prose.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Answer Span Optimization</b><span>Write the contiguous answer most likely to be surfaced.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Topical Authority</b><span>Map the topic, build the cluster, and link it correctly.</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="services">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Services</span>
            <h2>What I do across the SEO journey</h2>
            <p>I can own the strategy, coordinate the execution, build the supporting systems, and report the outcome—from the first audit to sustained growth.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card-grid">
          <article class="service feature">
            <div class="icon">01</div>
            <h3>Technical SEO</h3>
            <p>Fix crawl, indexation, rendering, structure, and speed issues across simple sites and huge inventories.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Crawl budget and index management</li>
              <li>Canonical, redirect, and sitemap strategy</li>
              <li>Core Web Vitals and JS rendering checks</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service feature">
            <div class="icon">02</div>
            <h3>Content Architecture</h3>
            <p>Design topical maps and pillar-cluster systems so content earns authority instead of competing with itself.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Search intent modeling</li>
              <li>Content gap and entity expansion</li>
              <li>Internal linking and page consolidation</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service feature">
            <div class="icon">03</div>
            <h3>Automation & Custom Tools</h3>
            <p>Turn repetitive SEO work into reliable workflows, scripts, dashboards, and internal tools that scale delivery.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>n8n, Python, Apps Script, and Colab workflows</li>
              <li>Custom SEO scripts, plugins, and extensions</li>
              <li>LLM-assisted analysis and QA systems</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">04</div>
            <h3>On-page SEO</h3>
            <p>Titles, metadata, headers, internal links, URLs, schema, and search-intent alignment.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Search-intent mapping</li>
              <li>Page-level optimization</li>
              <li>Internal linking</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">05</div>
            <h3>Off-page & Authority</h3>
            <p>Build trust beyond the page through white-hat links, digital PR, citations, and brand signals.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Link-building campaigns</li>
              <li>Backlink audits</li>
              <li>Digital PR and outreach</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">06</div>
            <h3>Content Writing</h3>
            <p>Write useful, intent-led content that is clear for readers and extractable for search systems.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>SEO briefs and copywriting</li>
              <li>Pillar and cluster content</li>
              <li>Answer-first content</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">07</div>
            <h3>Reporting & Analytics</h3>
            <p>Make performance visible through dashboards, KPI systems, and decision-ready reporting.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>GSC, GA4, and Looker Studio</li>
              <li>GTM and conversion tracking</li>
              <li>Weekly and monthly reporting</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">08</div>
            <h3>AI Search & LLM Tracking</h3>
            <p>Monitor how brands appear across AI answers while improving their semantic and structured-data foundations.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>AEO and GEO visibility</li>
              <li>LLM prompt and answer tracking</li>
              <li>Schema and llms.txt readiness</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="service compact">
            <div class="icon">09</div>
            <h3>Local & E-commerce SEO</h3>
            <p>Grow local and commerce properties through GBP, location pages, collections, products, and Merchant Center.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Local SEO and citations</li>
              <li>Shopify and collection SEO</li>
              <li>Facets, feeds, and schema</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="automation">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">SEO automation</span>
            <h2>Less repetitive work. More time for strategy.</h2>
            <p>I connect the SEO workflow from data collection to action, using the right level of automation for the job.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-grid">
          <article class="research-card" style="background:var(--text);color:#fff;border-color:var(--text)">
            <div class="label" style="color:var(--gold)">Automation stack</div>
            <h3>From n8n and Python to Apps Script and LLM workflows.</h3>
            <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.72)">I build small, useful systems that remove repetitive manual work without turning the process into a black box.</p>
            <div class="frameworks">
              <div class="framework"><b>n8n</b><span>Connect APIs, spreadsheets, alerts, and approvals into repeatable SEO workflows.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Python</b><span>Transform crawls, queries, content inventories, and performance data into decisions.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Apps Script</b><span>Extend Sheets and reporting systems with custom functions and scheduled jobs.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>LLM workflows</b><span>Support clustering, briefs, QA, entity extraction, and search-visibility tracking.</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="research-card">
            <div class="label">What gets automated</div>
            <h3>Automation across the SEO journey.</h3>
            <div class="frameworks">
              <div class="framework"><b>Discovery</b><span>Competitor collection, keyword normalization, crawl extraction, and opportunity lists.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Production</b><span>Brief generation, content checks, internal-link suggestions, and schema QA.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Monitoring</b><span>Rank, GSC, technical health, AI answers, and anomaly alerts.</span></div>
              <div class="framework"><b>Reporting</b><span>Automated dashboards, client-ready summaries, and action queues.</span></div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="industries">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
