    <section id="process">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">My process</span>
            <h2>My process moves from evidence to verified growth.</h2>
            <p>I keep the process clear enough for a team to follow and rigorous enough to support real decisions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process">
          <article class="step">
            <div class="num">1</div>
            <h3>Diagnose</h3>
            <p>Review Search Console, analytics, site structure, and technical signals to find what is actually limiting growth.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step">
            <div class="num">2</div>
            <h3>Architect</h3>
            <p>Map the topic, entity relationships, page types, and internal-link structure so the site has a coherent shape.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step">
            <div class="num">3</div>
            <h3>Implement</h3>
            <p>Apply the changes across templates, content, schema, crawl rules, and reporting systems.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step">
            <div class="num">4</div>
            <h3>Measure</h3>
            <p>Track gains, watch for regressions, and keep tuning the system as search behavior and algorithms shift.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="work">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div class="copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Case studies</span>
            <h2>Selected work backed by Search Console data</h2>
            <p>Client names are confidential; the verticals, approaches, and Search Console metrics are real.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="work-list">
          <article class="case">
            <div>
              <div class="case-top">
                <span class="case-id">Case 01</span>
                <span class="chipline">Health / YMYL recovery</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Recovered a large medical platform after a multi-update visibility drop.</h3>
              <p>
                Diagnosed the decline across core and spam updates, isolated duplicate-content risk,
                and rebuilt the recovery plan around content gaps, taxonomy, previously valuable URLs,
                and crawl-budget fixes.
              </p>
              <div class="case-feat">Included Screaming Frog audits, Googlebot rendering checks, and preparation for AI-search readiness.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-metrics">
              <div class="metric hero"><span>Hero metric</span><strong>21.2M clicks</strong><small>Health / YMYL recovery in 16 months</small></div>
              <div class="metric-row">
                <div class="metric small"><span>Impressions</span><strong>1.47B</strong><small>Search Console</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>CTR</span><strong>1.4%</strong><small>Average</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>Position</span><strong>7.3</strong><small>Average</small></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="case">
            <div>
              <div class="case-top">
                <span class="case-id">Case 02</span>
                <span class="chipline">Programmatic architecture</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Scaled a UK vehicle-scrapping service without letting pages go thin.</h3>
              <p>
                Built manufacturer landing pages from structured outlines, refined FAQs, and expanded into
                adjacent markets while tightening robots, schema, staging links, and backlink quality.
              </p>
              <div class="case-feat">This is the kind of project where the page template itself becomes part of the ranking strategy.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-metrics">
              <div class="metric hero"><span>Hero metric</span><strong>1.12M clicks</strong><small>Programmatic scale in 16 months</small></div>
              <div class="metric-row">
                <div class="metric small"><span>Impressions</span><strong>117M</strong><small>Search Console</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>CTR</span><strong>1%</strong><small>Average</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>Position</span><strong>14.8</strong><small>Average</small></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="case">
            <div>
              <div class="case-top">
                <span class="case-id">Case 03</span>
                <span class="chipline">Shopify / e-commerce</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Fixed crawl waste and rendering issues on a JavaScript-heavy Shopify store.</h3>
              <p>
                Reworked collection inventories, mapped product attributes, generated collection pages at scale,
                and enforced canonical, redirect, and pruning rules so crawl budget supported revenue pages.
              </p>
              <div class="case-feat">Aligned dynamic schema and Merchant Center signals to keep the catalog understandable to search systems.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-metrics">
              <div class="metric hero"><span>Hero metric</span><strong>449K clicks</strong><small>Shopify crawl / rendering fix in 16 months</small></div>
              <div class="metric-row">
                <div class="metric small"><span>Impressions</span><strong>40.8M</strong><small>Search Console</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>CTR</span><strong>1.1%</strong><small>Average</small></div>
                <div class="metric small"><span>Position</span><strong>8.2</strong><small>Average</small></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="case">
            <div>
              <div class="case-top">
                <span class="case-id">Case 04</span>
                <span class="chipline">Recovery and stability</span>
              </div>
              <h3>I stabilized a large site and created a stronger growth baseline.</h3>
              <p>I combined technical cleanup, content improvements, and ongoing measurement to lift output and create a more stable organic growth system.</p>
              <div class="case-feat">I focused on repeatable improvements rather than a short-term spike, with a clear step-change in early 2026.</div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-metrics">
              <div class="metric hero"><span>Hero metric</span><strong>60.4K clicks</strong><small>Recovery and stability over 16 months</small></div>
